# Example environment — copy to `.env` and fill in real values. Only variables introduced by the POS
# hardening work are documented here; the full set of required secrets lives in your deployed `.env`.

# ── POS plan entitlement rollout ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Gate for PosEntitlementGuard (src/pos/guards/pos-entitlement.guard.ts), which requires an active POS
# plan on the SELLING routes: open a session, create/hold/complete a sale, browse POS products. PIN login,
# session close, cash adjustments, refunds, voids and reports are never gated.
#
#   false (default, or unset) = REPORT-ONLY. Nothing is blocked; the guard logs a WARN line per request it
#                               WOULD have blocked ("[report-only] would block POST /api/pos/sales —
#                               store=<id> reason=<no plan|plan expired|store suspended>"). Use this to find
#                               stores still selling without a plan before turning enforcement on.
#   true                      = ENFORCE. Blocked requests get 403 {code:'POS_PLAN_REQUIRED'|'POS_STORE_DISABLED'}.
#
# Only the exact string "true" enforces. Roll out: deploy with false → review the warnings and run
# `src/scripts/pos-plan-backfill.ts` (dry run, then --grant) → set to true and restart.
POS_ENTITLEMENT_ENFORCED=false

# ── POS legacy auth sunset (Phase 5D.1) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# POS routes accept a registered DEVICE token (preferred) or, for installs that predate devices, the owner/staff JWT.
#   true (default) = legacy owner-JWT POS installs keep working; the app walks the owner through device setup on its own.
#   false          = owner/staff JWTs are refused on POS routes with 403 {code:'POS_LEGACY_AUTH_DISABLED'}; the app reacts by
#                    forcing "Set up this device" (cart and unsynced sales are kept). Flip it once all tills are registered.
# Note: this also applies to any web POS terminal that calls /api/pos with the owner session.
POS_LEGACY_AUTH_ALLOWED=true
